{"availability":"available","full":"amyrmahdy/decima","name":"decima","description":"Open, CPU-sized Jev-style (System One) decision model: situation + question + options → calibrated probabilities. 122M, ~20 ms on one CPU core, runs in your browser.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-27T12:12:35Z","updated":"2026-10-08T12:16:47Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["calibration","decision-model","jev","jev-alternative","multilingual","onnx","system-one","typed-decisions","zero-shot-classification"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/amyrmahdy/decima-playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:35.217Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Small local judges for LLM systems. Give Decima a situation, a question and your options; it returns calibrated probabilities in milliseconds, on a CPU, with nothing leaving your machine.","(Outputs shortened to the top answer per question; the CLI also prints the runners-up.)","Decima is the judge, not the writer. Put it next to your LLM, agent or extraction pipeline to decide what is safe, what is true, where a request should go, and when the expensive model is really needed. It speaks TypeSafe's /v1/systemone format (choice, noul, score), so code written for Jev works after a one-line change, and it ships in Ollaya."],"features":["Local and cheap: int8 ONNX, about 20–50 ms per decision on one CPU core. No GPU, no API key, no data leaves.","Calibrated: 0.8 means right about 80 % of the time, so you can threshold, abstain, or escalate to a bigger model.","Order-proof: shuffling the options never changes the answer (0 %; other open models in our tests: 10–27 %).","Your options, at call time: any labels, any number. Multilingual backbone; evaluated in 20 languages."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amyrmahdy/decima/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2c3fb95371c71eddd28c3e68184d00ed287bd2600db632553135f85e5058492f","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T18:02:18.821Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T18:02:18.821Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Small local judges for LLM systems. Give Decima a situation, a question and your options; it returns calibrated probabilities in milliseconds, on a CPU, with nothing leaving your machine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amyrmahdy/decima/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2c3fb95371c71eddd28c3e68184d00ed287bd2600db632553135f85e5058492f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amyrmahdy/decima/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:02:18.821Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T12:16:47Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/amyrmahdy/decima/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T18:02:18.822Z","hash":"2c3fb95371c71eddd28c3e68184d00ed287bd2600db632553135f85e5058492f","originalBytes":10923,"storedBytes":10923,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["decima","python","model","run","decima-agent","decima-base","items","runs","answer","int8","onnx","data","kev","suites","audit","every","integrations","models","one","out","presets","team","technical","bench.items","decima-small","examples","laya","mcp","triage","which","agent-gate","any","bash","billing","calib","code","cpu","export","first","item","jev","langchain","llm","local","options","per","predictions","preset","question","release","router","scripts","system","training","agent","api","btzsc","builders","calibrated","choice","command","decision","gate","gates","hooks","how","jabr","licensing.md","model.","never","noul","numbers","open","own","preds","report","repository","rules","sales","scores","server","small